title: Saved layouts
intro: The editor opens with the panels where you left them. Save layouts by name, switch between them, and reset to the start.
project: Platformer | Saved Layouts

chapter: Save a layout | View > Save Layout...
say: Say you like the Inspector on the left, with the Output log in a window of its own.
dock: Inspector > left
float: Output > 150, -60
expectlayout: Inspector | Hierarchy | (Documents / Assets, Profiler); floating: Output
explain: menu:View | Save it | The View menu saves where the panels are now, under a name of your choosing.
menu: View > Save Layout...
prompt: Level Building
say: Close the editor and it opens again just like this, floating windows and all, at the same size and place on screen. Saved layouts are yours, kept for every project you open.

chapter: Back to the start | View > Reset Layout
menu: View > Reset Layout
expectlayout: Hierarchy | (Documents / Assets, Output, Profiler) | Inspector
explain: panel:Inspector | Reset | Reset Layout puts every panel back where it starts out, and closes floating windows.

chapter: Switch layouts | View > Layouts
menu: View > Layouts > Level Building
expectlayout: Inspector | Hierarchy | (Documents / Assets, Profiler); floating: Output
explain: float:Output | Switched back | The Layouts menu lists every layout you've saved. Pick one, and the panels go where it has them.
menu: View > Delete Layout > Level Building
say: Delete Layout forgets one you no longer want. Agents can save, load and reset layouts too.
